# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Eleventy builds the blog into _site/, but the marketing pages (index.html,
# services.html, css/, images/) live at the repo root, so the Pages "build
# output directory" has to stay "/" and _site/ ends up as a subfolder of the
# deployed site. These rewrites hide that: /blog/... is served from
# /_site/blog/... with a 200, so the URL the visitor sees never changes.
#
# This is the Cloudflare equivalent of the [[redirects]] blocks in
# netlify.toml. Keep the two in sync until the Netlify site is retired --
# primeprowork.com still resolves to Netlify as of 2026-08-16.
#
# Exact paths first, then the splats: a request for /blog (no trailing slash)
# must not fall through to the SPA fallback, which is what serves the
# homepage -- with its root-relative links -- under the /blog/ prefix today.

/blog                 /_site/blog/                    200
/es/blog              /_site/es/blog/                 200
/sitemap.xml          /_site/sitemap.xml              200

/es/blog/*            /_site/es/blog/:splat           200
/blog/*               /_site/blog/:splat              200
